<header>
  <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/lesson38">JavaScript Course</a> &gt; Lesson 38 - Password Generator</p>
  <p><a id="homeLink" href="/">← Back to Home</a> | JavaScript Course - Lesson 38 / 50</p>
  <h1>Lesson 38: Password Generator - Strong Random Passwords</h1>
  <p>Math.random, Length, Copy Button, Strength Meter | LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</p>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <div class="tabs">
    <button id="lessonTabBtn" class="tab-btn active" onclick="showLesson()">📖 Lesson</button>
    <button id="testTabBtn" class="tab-btn" onclick="showTest()">📝 Test - 100 Marks</button>
  </div>
  <div id="lockMsg" class="lock-msg">🔒 Test is running! All tabs are locked until you submit the test or time ends.</div>

  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What Will We Build?</h2>
    <p>Today we build a <b>Password Generator</b> - A tool that creates strong random passwords. You choose length, tick what to include - Capital letters, Small letters, Numbers, Symbols - Click Generate, and get a new password every time. Plus a Copy button and a Strength Meter.</p>
    <p>This project uses: <b>Math.random()</b> for randomness, <b>Math.floor()</b> for whole numbers, <b>String charAt()</b> to pick a character, <b>Loop</b> to build password, <b>Checkbox</b> for options, <b>Clipboard</b> for copy.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>How It Works - 3 Steps:</b> 1. Build one big string of allowed characters - e.g. "ABC...abc...123...!@#". 2. Loop length times - Each time pick one random character from that string. 3. Join them - That is your password.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - Try Your Password Generator</h2>
    <p>Change length, tick options, generate, copy:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <div class="pass-wrap">
        <h3 style="text-align:center;margin:0 0 12px">🔐 Password Generator</h3>
        <div class="pass-output">
          <input id="passOut" type="text" value="Click Generate" readonly>
          <button onclick="copyPass()">📋 Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:13px;color:#cbd5e1"><span>Strength: <b id="strengthText">-</b></span><span id="copyMsg"></span></div>
        <div class="strength"><div class="strength-bar" id="strengthBar"></div></div>
        <div class="pass-row"><span>Password Length</span><span><input type="range" id="passLength" min="4" max="30" value="12" oninput="updateLengthLabel()"> <b id="lengthLabel">12</b></span></div>
        <div class="pass-row"><span>Include Capital Letters (A-Z)</span><input type="checkbox" id="optUpper" checked></div>
        <div class="pass-row"><span>Include Small Letters (a-z)</span><input type="checkbox" id="optLower" checked></div>
        <div class="pass-row"><span>Include Numbers (0-9)</span><input type="checkbox" id="optNumbers" checked></div>
        <div class="pass-row"><span>Include Symbols (!@#$%)</span><input type="checkbox" id="optSymbols" checked></div>
        <button class="btn btn-js" style="width:100%;font-size:18px" onclick="generatePass()">Generate Password 🔄</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h2>3. Step 1 - Math.random() - The Magic</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">console.log(Math.random()); // Any random decimal 0 to 0.999... e.g. 0.7342</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(Math.random() * 10); // 0 to 9.999...</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(Math.floor(Math.random() * 10)); // 0 to 9 - Whole number</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Formula - Random index for any string</span><br>
<span class="text">let chars = "ABCDEF"; // Length 6, indexes 0 to 5</span><br>
<span class="text">let randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * chars.length); // 0 to 5</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(chars[randomIndex]); // Random letter - e.g. "C"</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(chars.charAt(randomIndex)); // Same - charAt() also works</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Memory Trick:</b> <code>Math.floor(Math.random() * length)</code> = Random whole number from 0 to length-1. You will use this formula in every random project - Dice, Quotes, Passwords, Colors.</div>
    <h2>4. Step 2 - Build Character Pool From Checkboxes</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let pool = "";</span><br>
<span class="text">if (document.getElementById("upper").checked) { pool += "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ"; }</span><br>
<span class="text">if (document.getElementById("lower").checked) { pool += "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz"; }</span><br>
<span class="text">if (document.getElementById("numbers").checked) { pool += "0123456789"; }</span><br>
<span class="text">if (document.getElementById("symbols").checked) { pool += "!@#$%^&*()_+-=[]{}"; }</span><br><br>
<span class="text">if (pool === "") { alert("Please tick at least one option!"); return; }</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>5. Step 3 - Loop + Pick Random Characters</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">function generatePassword() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let length = 12; // From slider</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let pool = "ABC...abc...123...!@#"; // From Step 2</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let password = ""; // Start empty</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * pool.length);</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">password += pool.charAt(randomIndex); // Add one random char</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("output").value = password;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">console.log(password); // e.g. "aK9!xQ2#mZ8p"</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. Copy Button - navigator.clipboard</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">function copyPassword() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let pass = document.getElementById("output").value;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">navigator.clipboard.writeText(pass); // Copy to clipboard</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">alert("Copied: " + pass);</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <p><b>Old Way:</b> <code>input.select(); document.execCommand("copy");</code> - Still works, but new way <code>navigator.clipboard.writeText()</code> is cleaner.</p>
    <h2>7. Strength Meter - Simple Logic</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">function checkStrength(password) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let score = 0;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (password.length >= 8) score++;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (password.length >= 12) score++;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (/[A-Z]/.test(password)) score++; // Has capital?</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (/[0-9]/.test(password)) score++; // Has number?</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (/[^A-Za-z0-9]/.test(password)) score++; // Has symbol?</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (score <= 2) return "Weak 🔴";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (score <= 3) return "Medium 🟡";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">return "Strong 🟢";</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>8. Complete Example - Mini Generator</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;body&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"out"</span> <span class="attr">readonly</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"generate()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Generate</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;script&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function generate() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let chars = "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789!@#$%";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let password = "";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">password += chars.charAt(Math.floor(Math.random() * chars.length));</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("out").value = password;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/script&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span> <span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>9. Homework - Make It Better</h2>
    <p>In Playground, add these:</p>
    <p>1. Full Generator like demo - Length slider, 4 checkboxes, Copy button, Strength meter<br>2. History - Save last 5 generated passwords in a list below, click to copy again<br>3. Dice Roller - Use same Math.random formula - Button shows random dice 1 to 6 with emoji 🎲</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Math.random() = 0 to 0.999 random decimal | Math.floor(Math.random() * length) = Random index 0 to length-1 | pool = All allowed chars joined from checkboxes | Loop length times, pick random char, += to password | charAt(index) = Character at position | navigator.clipboard.writeText(text) = Copy | Strength = Length + Types - More types = Stronger</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> <a href="/lesson39">Lesson 39 - Weather App</a> - Learn API and fetch(). Show real weather of any city.</p>
    <a id="playgroundLink" class="btn" href="/playground">▶ Try it Yourself - Playground</a><br><br>
